<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.5.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00139</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.5.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>9f3c822a-5e76-4772-9739-75a91705b430</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <para>Use the graph for questions 1 - 2.</para> 
        <media alt="graph of (0, 4) and (4, 0).">
          <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_01_07_13_01.png" />
        </media>

        <exercise id="_3421aa35-b50d-4c5c-a3b1-441817c24a26" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Which of the following ordered pairs are on the line? Select <emphasis>three</emphasis>
              answers.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \((0, 4)\), \((2, 2)\), \((-2, 6)\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.5.3.</para>
            <para>The correct answers are \((0, 4)\), \((2, 2)\), \((-2, 6)\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

        <exercise id="_415975ee-822f-40eb-99ca-a1679c41d927" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Which of the following ordered pairs are solutions to the equation? Select <emphasis>
              three</emphasis> solutions.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \((0, 4)\), \((2, 2)\), \((-2, 6)\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.5.3.</para>
            <para>The correct answers are \((0, 4)\), \((2, 2)\), \((-2, 6)\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

        <para>For questions 3 and 4, use the graph of \(y = 3x -1\) as shown.</para>
              <media alt="">
                <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_01_07_13_02.png" />
              </media>

        <exercise id="_979c0e0d-259c-42cb-a28b-039132e7ceab" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Which of the following ordered pairs are on the line? Select <emphasis>three</emphasis>
              answers</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \((0, -1)\), \((1, 2)\), \((2, 5)\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.5.3.</para>
            <para>The correct answers are \((0, -1)\), \((1, 2)\), \((2, 5)\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

        <exercise id="_9be3c94b-b5fd-4db2-adf0-8aa79239490f" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Which of the following ordered pairs are solutions to the equation? Select <emphasis>
              three</emphasis> solutions.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \((0, -1)\), \((1, 2)\), \((2, 5)\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.5.3.</para>
            <para>The correct answers are \((0, -1)\), \((1, 2)\), \((2, 5)\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

        <exercise id="b0789d3d-017e-4fdf-9a8c-8a3f136c5cab" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Which of the following ordered pairs are solutions to the equation? Select <emphasis>
              three</emphasis> solutions.</para>
              <media alt="">
                <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_01_07_13_03.png" />
              </media>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \((-4, -3)\), \((-1, 1.5)\), \((0, 3)\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.5.3.</para>
            <para>The correct answers are \((-4, -3)\), \((-1, 1.5)\), \((0, 3)\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

        <exercise id="d5a98fb8-d5a5-4373-9325-cf4e7dd62f4d" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Here is a graph of the equation \( x+3y=6 \).</para>            
            <para>Select three coordinate pairs that represent a solution to the equation.</para>
              <media alt="">
                <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_01_07_13_04.png" />
              </media>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \((0, 2)\), \((3, 1)\), \((6, 0)\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.5.3.</para>
            <para>The correct answers are \((0, 2)\), \((3, 1)\), \((6, 0)\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content>
